  "_comment": "Battle batch 2026-10g, applied by scripts/add-battles-batch-2026-10g.mjs. Read from Wikidata (WDQS) on 26 Oct 2026: the pin is the item's single P625 on Earth (Q2), the year is its P585 (or the earliest P580 if it has no P585) recorded to at least the year (BC years converted from WDQS's astronomical numbering, so -0326 means 327 BC), endYear is the latest P582 when it falls in a later year, partOf is P361, sides are P710 where Wikidata names two or three, notability is the sitelink count, name and wikiTitle are the English Wikipedia article title. Wikidata records no winner (P1346) for any of these, so no result is given; English Wikipedia could not be read from the machine that made this batch. Pins that are whole degrees or sit on the country's own P625 point were left out, and every pin was checked by eye against the place named in the title. These come from the four-to-five sitelink band (nearly every battle with more is already on file), picked from well-known wars and the thin parts of the globe: Africa, the Middle East and Caucasus, Central Asia, South and Southeast Asia, Japan and Korea, the Americas before 1800, Oceania (New Zealand, Hawaii, Samoa), and ancient and early medieval Europe. Every battle was checked against events.json and battles.json by Q-id and by name within a year, and against the skipped lists of the earlier batches.",
